findings.evidence:
// The composite disclosure header retains Core shadow styling. Managed
// fields and action buttons preserve decoration allowance while disabled;
// their layout must not revert to the old disabled-state shrinkage.

findings.suggestion:
Lift the expectations into a named slice and derive the displacement from its sum so the two assertions cannot drift apart:

```go
shrinks := []int{6, 0, 0}
for i, shrink := range shrinks {
    if normalHeights[i]-disabledHeights[i] != shrink {
        t.Fatal("disabled style metric", dpi, i, normalHeights, disabledHeights)
    }
}
disabledDelta := 0
for _, shrink := range shrinks {
    disabledDelta += shrink
}
if find("section-after").Bounds.Min.Y != afterY-disabledDelta {
    t.Fatal("disabled section layout", dpi, afterY, find("section-after").Bounds)
}
```

